@page "/restaurant-demo"

<PageTitle>A restaurant's agent · louis-agent</PageTitle>
<PageHead Description="Watch a restaurant's website agent answer a family about Sunday lunch and pass their table request on, recorded once and played back." />

<BusinessDemo Kicker="A restaurant" Business="Wheatfield Kitchen" Title="wheatfieldkitchen.example · the agent in the corner" Turns="Conversation"
              Heading="A table for Sunday, at ten at night."
              Lede="A family of five asks Wheatfield Kitchen about Sunday lunch, long after the kitchen has closed. The agent answers from what the owner told it, and passes the table on.">
    <Points>
        <li><strong>It knows the restaurant.</strong> The hours, the menu and its prices, the stoep and the parking, from a few files the owner can change.</li>
        <li><strong>It never promises a table.</strong> It can't see the bookings, so it takes the request and the owner confirms.</li>
        <li><strong>It asks before it sends.</strong> The details go to the owner only after the family says yes.</li>
    </Points>
</BusinessDemo>
